<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 56,009 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 56,009 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 56,009 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7.00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 30,102 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Monday	September 14</p>
<p>Export cargo 4,845 771</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  51,164     29,331</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, three were expected to sail and seven were expected to arrive.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Sugar		    2,500	  Neijiang	     18/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		 8,000	  Strength	     21/9</p>
<p>Gas oil		  56,000	 Keefan		 21/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
